| 2.3 | `app.listen` (line 19) | The `listen` call has no error callback. A port-conflict or permission error will crash the process silently (or with an unformatted exception). | `app.listen(3000, () => {...}).on('error', (err) => { console.error('Server failed to start', err); process.exit(1); });` |

---

### 3. Security

| # | Location | Issue | Fix |
|---|----------|-------|-----|
| 3.1 | `GET /health` (line 7) | `new Date().toISOString()` in a public endpoint leaks the server's current clock with millisecond precision — useful for timing attacks. | Omit the timestamp, or only expose it to authenticated/internal callers. |
| 3.2 | `GET /users` (line 12) | User data (names + emails) is returned to **any** caller with no authentication or authorisation check. | Add an auth middleware (JWT, session, API key) before this route. |
| 3.3 | Entire file | No HTTP security headers. Default Express responses advertise `X-Powered-By: Express`. | Add `helmet` (`app.use(require('helmet')())`) — it sets CSP, HSTS, removes `X-Powered-By`, etc. in one line. |
| 3.4 | Entire file | No rate limiting. The `/users` endpoint (and any future endpoints) can be scraped or brute-forced freely. | Add `express-rate-limit` as a global or per-route middleware. |
| 3.5 | Entire file | No CORS policy defined. In a browser context the default is permissive and context-dependent. | Use the `cors` package with an explicit `origin` allowlist. |
| 3.6 | `app.listen` (line 19) | Port `3000` is hardcoded. Running as a non-root user is good, but the port (and other config) should come from environment variables. | `const PORT = process.env.PORT ?? 3000;` |

---

### Minimal Hardened Skeleton

```js
const express = require('express');
const helmet  = require('helmet');
const rateLimit = require('express-rate-limit');
const cors    = require('cors');

const app  = express();
const PORT = process.env.PORT ?? 3000;

// Security headers
app.use(helmet());

// CORS – replace with your actual origin(s)
app.use(cors({ origin: process.env.ALLOWED_ORIGIN ?? 'https://yourapp.example.com' }));

// Body parsing
app.use(express.json({ limit: '10kb' }));

// Rate limiting
app.use(rateLimit({ windowMs: 60_000, max: 100 }));

// Auth middleware placeholder
const requireAuth = (req, res, next) => {
  // verify JWT / session here
  next();
};

app.get('/health', (req, res) => {
  res.json({ status: 'ok' }); // timestamp removed
});

app.get('/users', requireAuth, (req, res) => {
  res.json([
    { id: 1, name: 'Alice', email: 'alice@example.com' },
    { id: 2, name: 'Bob',   email: 'bob@example.com'  },
  ]);
});

// 404 handler
app.use((req, res) => res.status(404).json({ error: 'Not found' }));

// Central error handler
app.use((err, req, res, _next) => {
  console.error(err);
  res.status(500).json({ error: 'Internal server error' });
});

app.listen(PORT, () => console.log(`Server running on port ${PORT}`))
   .on('error', (err) => { console.error(err); process.exit(1); });

module.exports = app;
```

